I've written the plan for Day 236 (19:46): two task files and an issue-responses file in session_plan/. The commit didn't happen because session_plan/ is gitignored. The instruction's || true allows for that, so the harness reads the files straight from disk.

Task 1: Part of #1062 (product, self-driven). When the API rejects a key with a 401, yoyo currently says OPENAI_API_KEY is not set even if the user passed --api-key. That's because diagnose_api_error (src/prompt_retry.rs) only checks that one environment variable. The fix:
• Record the key's source: keep a note of where this session's key came from (--api-key, config file, or which environment variable), the same way the provider is already recorded.
• New message per source: a small, table-tested helper picks the message. When no key is found anywhere, the message must stay word-for-word what it is today.
• Alias names: for names like GEMINI_API_KEY, reuse the helper added on Day 235 for #1064 rather than writing a second list.
• Before/after check: run it against a local server that always answers 401 and paste both outputs into the commit.

This deliberately stays out of src/main.rs, because the trajectory flagged that area as over-worked lately. The setup-wizard half of #1062 is left open, so the title says "Part of", not "Fixes".

Task 2: Part of #944 (evolve, backlog slot for the oldest open issue). Today's two #944 changes made the social and dream runs record their spend on the audit-log branch. I fetched that branch while planning: social already has real entries (one run: $1.25 on claude-opus-5-5). Dream has none yet because it runs every 7 days. Nothing reads these records yet, so the task adds a "Phase spend" section to extract_trajectory.py. Each phase shows one of three states:
• Has entries: totals, labelled as a minimum because sub-agent tokens aren't counted.
• No entries yet: said as such.
• Branch couldn't be read: says "could not check".

After that, a comment on #944 lists what's left:
• `daily_diary.sh`: no workflow calls it, so it only gets run by hand.
• `synthesize.yml`: I can't edit it, so it needs @yuanhao.
• Sub-agent tokens: the fix has to come from yoagent (yoagent#173).

